# Git sync before work

When you begin substantive work in a git repository, run once from the repository root:

`bash "$HOME/.claude/hooks/git-sync-main.sh"`

The script reads `cwd` from JSON on stdin when not a TTY (same as Claude/Codex hooks). From a normal shell in the repo, run it with no stdin so it uses the current directory. It fetches `origin` and fast-forwards `main` or `master` only when that branch is checked out; other branches are unchanged aside from the fetch.
